# The sources plinux actually builds. One line per entry in packages/order,
# in the same order.
#
# This is not the LFS list. wget-list-sysv is the book's own file and is 91
# entries, of which about sixty are the temporary toolchain -- gcc, binutils,
# gmp, mpfr, mpc, m4, make, perl, python, tcl, expect, autoconf, libtool,
# texinfo -- that LFS builds in chapters 5 and 6 so that chapter 8 can be
# built inside a chroot. plinux does none of that: it builds against the host
# toolchain and stages into obj/, so downloading those tarballs fetches
# several hundred megabytes that nothing ever unpacks.
#
# wget-list-sysv is kept in the tree, unused by default, because it is the
# starting point if the self-hosting toolchain ever gets built. Fetch it with
# ./download.sh --list wget-list-sysv.
#
# Four things the build needs are not here, because they do not come from a
# tarball: the kernel and pboot are git checkouts under src/, and src/musl
# and src/bash were unpacked by hand and have no recorded origin.

# the C libraries. glibc first: udev is part of systemd and systemd does not
# build against musl, so both are installed and every binary names the one
# it wants.
https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/glibc/glibc-2.42.tar.xz
https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/lfs/12.4/glibc-2.42-fhs-1.patch

